---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { AUTHOR, CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL_UPDATED } from "../consts";
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What Teximos collects, what it does not, and who to contact.">
  <div class="page">
    <div class="shell">
      <span class="kicker">Privacy</span>
      <h1>What happens to your data</h1>

      <div class="prose column">
        <p>
          Teximos is a publication. It does not have accounts, it does not ask
          you for anything, and it does not sell or share personal data. This
          page sets out what the site does and does not do. It was last updated
          on {LEGAL_UPDATED}.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing, from you directly. There are no sign up forms, no comment
          boxes and no newsletter. Reading a piece does not ask you to give
          us anything.
        </p>
        <p>
          The one thing a reader might choose to store is a colour theme. If
          you switch between light, dark and system, that choice is kept in
          your own browser and is never sent to us.
        </p>

        <h2>Search</h2>
        <p>
          The archive search runs in your browser against a search index that
          is published with the site. Your queries are not sent anywhere.
        </p>

        <h2>Hosting and server logs</h2>
        <p>
          Teximos is hosted and served by Cloudflare. Like any website, the
          hosting provider keeps standard request logs, which typically include
          an IP address, the time of the request, the page requested and the
          browser or client that made it. Those logs are used to keep the site
          online and secure. Cloudflare's own handling of that data is set out
          in its privacy policy at cloudflare.com/privacypolicy.
        </p>

        <h2>Analytics and advertising</h2>
        <p>
          Teximos does not run analytics and does not show advertising. There
          are no tracking scripts and no third party scripts on any page. If
          that ever changes, this page will be updated first and the change
          will be dated.
        </p>

        <h2>Email</h2>
        <p>
          If you write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>,
          we keep your message and your address only so that we can reply and
          fix whatever you raised. We do not add you to any list.
        </p>

        <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
        <p>
          Pieces link to primary sources, company announcements, agency releases
          and papers. Those sites have their own privacy practices, which we do
          not control.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          Teximos is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly
          collect information from them.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Because we do not hold personal data about readers, there is usually
          nothing to access, correct or delete. If you believe we hold something
          about you, write to us at the address above and we will answer. Readers
          in California and the European Economic Area have rights over personal
          data, and you can ask us about them at any time.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If this page changes, the date at the top changes with it.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this page go to
          <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. {AUTHOR.name}
          runs Teximos.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
</content>
